## Progress

- 2026-10-26: Goal written from the audit's lanes 9 and 10.

- 2026-10-27 08:09 UTC: All five items done. Item 1: `liveText` in `src/core/live.ts` cuts a line over 8,000 characters and marks it `[cut]`, for the harness's own lines and every program's; a Pi session's refused line is logged, the first of a streak (`tests/harness/agents/live-session.test.ts`). Item 2: the supervisor names the commands it holds (`have`), and control answers those with their ids alone (`pendingFor` in `src/control/issue.ts`; `tests/supervisor/relay.test.ts` measures each fetch). Item 3: control verifies a live batch's signature over its lines as sent, keeps the lines it knows and counts the rest under `left_out`, and the supervisor logs each once (`src/control/live-in.ts`, which also shrinks `api.ts`; `tests/control/live.test.ts`). Item 4: OpenCode takes its prompt on stdin (OpenCode 2.1.4 in the harness image takes a piped message: checked offline in the image), and Claude Code reads it from a file in the run's own folder on stdin, the token staying on descriptor 3 (`tests/harness/agents/claude-code.test.ts` sends a 200,000-character prompt through the shell; `tests/harness/agents/opencode.test.ts`). Item 5: the test showed it: an assignment whose sources stage longer than its life expired. Now the supervisor names what still stages (`staging`), and control signs such a command again with a later expiry within 10 minutes of it, at most 24 hours after it was issued, with `command_renewed` in the audit log (`tests/supervisor/relay.test.ts`, which fails without it). The pages follow. The fast checks and the agents, Claude Code and steering acceptance checks are left.
